Retain the host-code sub-libraries in a shared build

cc_shared_library whole-archives only its direct deps, so the seventeen host
sub-libraries whose symbols only app-side Swift references would be dropped by
lazy archive linking. alwayslink keeps them. The four cuda_library targets are
deliberately left lazy, because their members ride the registrant references in
the committed ccv_nnc_cmd.inc and forcing them would embed hundreds of
megabytes of kernels the binaries never carried. nnc_headers stays lazy for the
same kind of reason, so its co.c does not force a second coroutine-TLS copy
into every consumer.

nnc_dynamic_headers exports the same header, define and include surface the
static ccv and nnc targets hand their consumers, including the bare sqlite3.h
include path from @sqlite3 on Linux. It is the interface of s4nnc's
ccv_nnc_dynamic and nothing more.
